  "body": "The header menu has some outdated links referring to m.org\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/blob/fca171427f11233cb1b82982ac541dd206ebbff8/config/_default/hugo.toml#L24-L35\n\n- the page about the foundation now lives at https://matrix.org/foundation/about/ since we introduced additional about pages for the GB and WGs. not a huge issue since a redirect from the old path is in place for now.\n- the FAQ page has been moved to https://matrix.org/docs/older/faq/ for a while (I think at least since the m.org homepage switched to zola). A redirect is also in place, however there is a big banner at the top that screams at the viewer \"uhm this is actually outdated\". Perhaps https://matrix.org/docs/ would be the appropriate replacement?\n  - as another really small nit, the page on m.org is called FAQ, not FAQs ;)\n- the blog is at https://matrix.org/blog/, presumably also since zola. Again a redirect is currently in place.\n\nIs this a change you would like the website WG to PR to the spec?",
